{"name":"Emerging Taupe","hex":"#b8a196","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"emerging","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Becoming prominent; emergent; rising."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of emerge"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/emerging"},{"term":"taupe","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dark brownish-grey colour, the colour of moleskin."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a dark brownish-grey colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/taupe"}],"entries":[{"title":"Emerging","blocks":[{"text":"Emerging is the title of the only album by the Phil Keaggy Band, released in 1977 on NewSong Records. The album's release was delayed due to a shift in record pressing plant priorities following the death of Elvis Presley. The album was re-released on CD in 2000 as ReEmerging with one original track omitted and four newly recorded songs by the band members."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/db/Phil_KeaggyEmerging1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emerging"},{"title":"Taupe","blocks":[{"text":"Taupe is a dark gray-brown color. The word derives from the French noun taupe meaning \"mole\". The name originally referred only to the average color of the French mole, but beginning in the 1940s, its usage expanded to encompass a wider range of shades."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taupe"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6f/Re-Emerging_%28Phil_Keaggy_Band_album_-_cover_art%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6f/Re-Emerging_%28Phil_Keaggy_Band_album_-_cover_art%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEmergi